{:mulog/duration 111375, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.event-store-v3.core.in-memory", :grain/event-ids (#uuid "019e431e-b4f3-70a6-82bd-3622e2953cdd" #uuid "019e431e-b4f3-70a7-9c71-18daa687e393" #uuid "019e431e-b4f2-707f-a58b-b809b0d989b4"), :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace #mulog/flake "5A3Yeolz3hivh2kya73dt6eIVRwK0yXn", :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3Yeolz3hivh2kya73dt6eIVRwK0yXn", :mulog/timestamp 1779242546419, :metric/name "GrainAppendEvents", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YeomPWYBQlRWxgMi6Qx4PXo68eQo_", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.event-store-v3.core.in-memory/append}
{:mulog/duration 1964666, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core/command {:tick-id #uuid "d50d8ccd-b92b-4a8a-846f-f40935f5c91c", :writes {:major-changes "Based on the comparison between microFIT v2.0 and v3.1.1, the changes are classified as follows:\n\n**MAJOR (Legal/Financial Impact):**\n*   **Removal of Domestic Content Requirements:** Complete elimination of the 60% Minimum Required Domestic Content Level (Section B(5)(iv), Section 4.4.4, and Appendix C).\n*   **Expansion of OPA Discretion on Project Eligibility:** Modification allowing the OPA \"sole and absolute discretion\" to consent to facilities that previously reached commercial operation (Appendix A).\n*   **Expanded Metadata Disclosure:** New provision allowing OPA to disclose facility data to government agencies for public health, safety, and emergency response (Section 6.5).\n\n**MINOR (Clarification/Administrative):**\n*   **Mandatory \"Prescribed Form\":** Requirement to use specific OPA-provided forms for contact changes, terminations, and amendments (Sections 5.1.2, 7.2, 8.1, 9 and Appendix A).\n*   **Definition of \"Existing Building\":** Clarification that OPA may manually deem a structure as an \"Existing Building\" (Appendix C).\n*   **Definition of \"Website\":** Explicitly defining the OPA program URL (Appendix A).\n\n**COSMETIC (Formatting):**\n*   **Renumbering:** Adjustments to subsection numbers following the removal of Domestic Content warranties (Section 4.4).\n*   **Typographical:** Addition of a space in \"orders- in-council\" (Appendix E).", :impact-analysis "| Major Change | Affected Party | Risk Shift & Impact Analysis |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Removal of Domestic Content Requirements** | **Supplier** | **Significant Risk Reduction for Supplier:** Suppliers are no longer bound by the complex and costly requirement to source 60% of components from Ontario. This lowers capital expenditures (CAPEX) and eliminates the legal/financial risk of contract termination for failing to meet hardware origin quotas. |\n| **Removal of Domestic Content Requirements** | **OPA** | **Shift of Policy Burden:** The OPA loses the ability to use the microFIT program as a direct tool for local economic development/manufacturing mandates. Administrative burden is reduced as they no longer need to audit supply chain origins. |\n| **Discretionary Eligibility for Existing Facilities** | **Supplier** | **Increased Flexibility:** Potential Suppliers with existing assets gain a pathway to contract eligibility that was previously barred, provided they obtain written OPA consent. |\n| **Mandatory \"Prescribed Form\" Usage** | **Supplier** | **Increased Administrative Rigor:** Suppliers face a higher risk of notice rejection/invalidity if they use custom correspondence instead of the specific forms hosted on the OPA website. |\n| **Safety/Emergency Data Disclosure** | **Supplier** | **Privacy/Operational Impact:** Suppliers must accept that their facility details will be shared with third-party government agencies. While intended for safety, it broadens the scope of data exposure compared to v2.0. |"}, :command/name :sheet/complete-node-execution, :command/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:02:26.417967-05:00", :command/id #uuid "2473fe08-af84-4643-8e30-6f6298e25467", :duration-ms 11496, :usage {:prompt-tokens 1009, :completion-tokens 661, :total-tokens 1670}, :status :success, :node-id #uuid "f3d2709f-d7b1-4709-8ea9-1d31bab67d8f", :sheet-id #uuid "b6096d4a-c55a-4e59-9948-bbefda19edda"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3Yeolz3hivh2kya73dt6eIVRwK0yXn", :mulog/timestamp 1779242546417, :metric/name "CommandProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3Yeolz3hivh2kya73dt6eIVRwK0yXn", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core/process-command, :metric/resolution :high}
