{:mulog/parent-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YeoocE9ytrMyLeTe1YLIQ0jiIlvbW", :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YeoocE9ytrMyLeTe1YLIQ0jiIlvbW", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YeoqWwvEC4Rku8Fy-qsO22NRPXAJ0", :mulog/timestamp 1779242546437, :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/anomaly-in-todo-processor, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :anomaly {:cognitect.anomalies/category :cognitect.anomalies/fault, :cognitect.anomalies/message "Todo Processor returned nil: %s"}}
{:mulog/parent-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YeooYCYZsM5ALf00ngX61PZQxp0O1", :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YeooYCYZsM5ALf00ngX61PZQxp0O1", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YeoqWsRljWkVxAxl21bmNJMbSi7l4", :mulog/timestamp 1779242546437, :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/anomaly-in-todo-processor, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :anomaly {:cognitect.anomalies/category :cognitect.anomalies/fault, :cognitect.anomalies/message "Todo Processor returned nil: %s"}}
{:mulog/duration 7986500, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :event {:tick-id #uuid "d50d8ccd-b92b-4a8a-846f-f40935f5c91c", :event/tags #{[:sheet #uuid "b6096d4a-c55a-4e59-9948-bbefda19edda"] [:tick #uuid "d50d8ccd-b92b-4a8a-846f-f40935f5c91c"] [:node #uuid "621a078e-88c6-4c70-9f3f-957b334f0e87"]}, :event/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:02:26.428307-05:00", :inputs {:document-survey "### Comparison of Contract Structures: microFIT v2.0 vs. v3.1.1\n\n| Section/Appendix | Status in v3.1.1 | Key Changes / Observations |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Part 1: Contract Details** | Retained | Structural parity. Section B(5)(iv) regarding Domestic Content removed. |\n| **Part 2: Terms and Conditions** | Retained | Minor wording updates; addition of \"Prescribed Form\" requirements for notices. |\n| **Section 1: Term** | Retained | No change. |\n| **Section 2: Pricing and Payment** | Retained | No change. |\n| **Section 3: Env. Attributes** | Retained | No change. |\n| **Section 4: Reps and Warranties** | Modified | **Removed:** v2 Section 4.4.4 (Domestic Content requirement). |\n| **Section 5: Covenants** | Modified | Added requirement for \"Prescribed Form\" for contact changes (5.1.2). |\n| **Section 6: General Conditions** | Modified | Section 6.5 (Disclosure) expanded to include health/safety and emergency services. |\n| **Section 7: Notices** | Modified | Added \"Prescribed Form\" requirement for changing contact info (7.2). |\n| **Section 8: Termination** | Modified | Added \"Prescribed Form\" requirement for Supplier termination (8.1). |\n| **Section 9: Amendment** | Modified | Added \"Prescribed Form\" requirement. |\n| **Section 10: Assignment** | Retained | No change. |\n| **Section 11: Governing Law** | Retained | No change. |\n| **Section 12: Dispute Resolution** | Retained | No change. |\n| **Section 13: LDC Failure to Pay** | Retained | No change. |\n| **Section 14: Multiple Entities** | Retained | No change. |\n| **Appendix A: Definitions** | Modified | **New terms:** \"Prescribed Form\", \"Website\". **Removed:** \"Domestic Content Level\", \"Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\". |\n| **Appendix B: Indexing** | Retained | No change. |\n| **Appendix C: Solar PV** | **REDUCED** | **Major Change:** In v3.1.1, the \"Domestic Content Requirements\" (Sections 1.1–1.7) and the three Domestic Content Grid Tables are **entirely removed**. |\n| **Appendix D-1: Directly Conn.** | Retained | No change. |\n| **Appendix D-2: Indirectly Conn.** | Retained | No change. |\n| **Appendix E: LDC Supplier** | Retained | No change. |\n\n**Summary of Key Structural Differences:**\n1.  **Domestic Content Removal:** The most significant change in Version 3.1.1 is the total removal of Domestic Content requirements. This includes the removal of specific warranties in Part 2 and the deletion of multiple pages of technical grids/rules in Appendix C.\n2.  **Prescribed Forms:** Version 3.1.1 introduces a standardized administrative process by requiring \"Prescribed Forms\" (defined in Appendix A) for notifications, terminations, and amendments.\n3.  **Expanded Information Sharing:** Section 6.5 in Version 3.1.1 adds provisions allowing the OPA to share facility data with emergency services and public health officials for safety planning.", :section-diffs "### Clause-by-Clause Comparison: microFIT v2.0 vs. v3.1.1\n\n#### Part 1 – Contract Details\n*   **Section B(5)(iv):** (Removal) Provision requiring a \"Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\" of 60% has been removed in v3.1.1.\n\n#### Part 2 – General Terms and Conditions\n*   **Section 4.4.4:** (Removal) Warranty stating that solar photovoltaic facilities must have a Domestic Content Level greater than or equal to the Minimum Required Domestic Content Level has been removed. *Subsequent subsections in v3.1.1 (formerly 4.4.5 and 4.4.6) have been renumbered to 4.4.4 and 4.4.5.*\n*   **Section 5.1.2:** (Modification) Added requirement that changes to Supplier contact information must be submitted in the **\"Prescribed Form\"**.\n*   **Section 6.5 (Collection/Disclosure of Information):** (Addition)\n    *   **Collection:** Removed \"information to establish compliance with Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\" from the list of data OPA may collect from third parties.\n    *   **Disclosure:** Added a new provision allowing OPA to disclose facility and location details to \"other government ministries, agencies, institutions or organizations\" for purposes of **public health and safety** and for **emergency services personnel** to plan for and respond to emergencies. \n*   **Section 7.2:** (Modification) Specifically requires that a change of contact information notice must be in the **\"Prescribed Form\"**.\n*   **Section 8.1:** (Modification) Requires Supplier termination notices to be in the **\"Prescribed Form\"**.\n*   **Section 9:** (Modification) Requires amendments or modifications to be reduced to writing in the **\"Prescribed Form\"**.\n\n#### Appendix A – Definitions\n*   **\"Domestic Content Level\":** (Removal) Definition deleted.\n*   **\"Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\":** (Removal) Definition deleted.\n*   **\"Prescribed Form\":** (Addition) New definition: \"means, in relation to a form, the latest version of the corresponding form appearing on the Website...\"\n*   **\"Website\":** (Addition) New definition: \"means the OPA’s Renewable Energy Feed-In Tariff Program website at 'http://microfit.powerauthority.on.ca'...\"\n*   **\"Project Eligibility Requirements (c)\":** (Modification) Added \"unless otherwise consented to by the OPA in writing in its sole and absolute discretion\" regarding facilities that have previously reached commercial operation.\n\n#### Appendix C – Solar Photovoltaic Schedule\n*   **Defined Term \"Existing Building\":** (Modification) Expanded to include buildings for which the OPA has issued written confirmation (at its sole discretion) that the building is deemed an \"Existing Building\".\n*   **Domestic Content Requirements (Sections 1.1 through 1.7):** (Removal) Entire section deleted, including rules for calculating Qualifying Percentages and requirements for evidence.\n*   **Tables 1, 2, and 3:** (Removal) The \"Domestic Content Grids\" for Crystalline Silicon, Thin-Film, and Concentrated PV Technologies (pages 17-19 of v2.0) are completely removed in v3.1.1.\n\n#### Appendix E – LDC Supplier Schedule\n*   **Section 3.1(a):** (Typographical Modification) Changed \"orders-in-council\" to \"orders- in-council\" (added a space).", :major-changes "Based on the comparison between microFIT v2.0 and v3.1.1, the changes are classified as follows:\n\n**MAJOR (Legal/Financial Impact):**\n*   **Removal of Domestic Content Requirements:** Complete elimination of the 60% Minimum Required Domestic Content Level (Section B(5)(iv), Section 4.4.4, and Appendix C).\n*   **Expansion of OPA Discretion on Project Eligibility:** Modification allowing the OPA \"sole and absolute discretion\" to consent to facilities that previously reached commercial operation (Appendix A).\n*   **Expanded Metadata Disclosure:** New provision allowing OPA to disclose facility data to government agencies for public health, safety, and emergency response (Section 6.5).\n\n**MINOR (Clarification/Administrative):**\n*   **Mandatory \"Prescribed Form\":** Requirement to use specific OPA-provided forms for contact changes, terminations, and amendments (Sections 5.1.2, 7.2, 8.1, 9 and Appendix A).\n*   **Definition of \"Existing Building\":** Clarification that OPA may manually deem a structure as an \"Existing Building\" (Appendix C).\n*   **Definition of \"Website\":** Explicitly defining the OPA program URL (Appendix A).\n\n**COSMETIC (Formatting):**\n*   **Renumbering:** Adjustments to subsection numbers following the removal of Domestic Content warranties (Section 4.4).\n*   **Typographical:** Addition of a space in \"orders- in-council\" (Appendix E).", :impact-analysis "| Major Change | Affected Party | Risk Shift & Impact Analysis |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Removal of Domestic Content Requirements** | **Supplier** | **Significant Risk Reduction for Supplier:** Suppliers are no longer bound by the complex and costly requirement to source 60% of components from Ontario. This lowers capital expenditures (CAPEX) and eliminates the legal/financial risk of contract termination for failing to meet hardware origin quotas. |\n| **Removal of Domestic Content Requirements** | **OPA** | **Shift of Policy Burden:** The OPA loses the ability to use the microFIT program as a direct tool for local economic development/manufacturing mandates. Administrative burden is reduced as they no longer need to audit supply chain origins. |\n| **Discretionary Eligibility for Existing Facilities** | **Supplier** | **Increased Flexibility:** Potential Suppliers with existing assets gain a pathway to contract eligibility that was previously barred, provided they obtain written OPA consent. |\n| **Mandatory \"Prescribed Form\" Usage** | **Supplier** | **Increased Administrative Rigor:** Suppliers face a higher risk of notice rejection/invalidity if they use custom correspondence instead of the specific forms hosted on the OPA website. |\n| **Safety/Emergency Data Disclosure** | **Supplier** | **Privacy/Operational Impact:** Suppliers must accept that their facility details will be shared with third-party government agencies. While intended for safety, it broadens the scope of data exposure compared to v2.0. |"}, :node-id #uuid "621a078e-88c6-4c70-9f3f-957b334f0e87", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-started, :sheet-id #uuid "b6096d4a-c55a-4e59-9948-bbefda19edda", :event/id #uuid "019e431e-b4fc-7041-acd4-256e1fb815d9"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YeoocE9ytrMyLeTe1YLIQ0jiIlvbW", :mulog/timestamp 1779242546429, :metric/name "TodoProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YeoocE9ytrMyLeTe1YLIQ0jiIlvbW", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/processing-event, :metric/resolution :high}
